# --- Python ---
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

# --- Local environment (copy .env.example -> .env) ---
# Every .env variant is ignored, not just the exact name: a backup made before
# rotating a credential (.env.bak, .env.local, .env.2026-07-29) holds the same
# live token as the original, and a rule that names only `.env` does not stop it
# being committed. The example file is the one deliberate exception.
.env*
!.env.example

# --- Credentials: never commit ---
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*

# --- Runtime output: regenerated by the tools; not part of the deliverable ---
# (see data/README.md).
data/*
!data/README.md

# --- Result data ------------------------------------------------------------
# results/ holds your own runs and is excluded on purpose, not by accident.
#
# The study's result artefacts are excluded on purpose too, which is a different
# decision and worth writing down. They are data for the paper, not code for the
# testbed: 8,550 verdicts in the multi-seed run alone, none of it useful to
# someone judging their own canaries. They are archived separately, and the DOI
# goes in the README once the article is published. Unpacking that archive back
# into this working tree must
# not make it committable by accident, so the reference directories are named
# here even though this repository does not contain them.
#
# An earlier version of this file used a blanket `/results/` rule and then tried
# to re-include two subdirectories under it. That does not work: git does not
# descend into a directory excluded by a directory rule, so the negations were
# never reached and the repository silently did not contain artefacts its own
# Data Availability Statement named. If you ever do need to track something under
# results/, exclude with `/results/*` and negate the subdirectory — the trailing
# `*` is what makes the negation reachable.
/results/
/reference-results/
/data-archive/

# example-results/ is the exception and is deliberately NOT ignored: it is a
# small committed slice that `make demo` renders from, so a fresh clone can run
# the analysis and figure path with no stack, no model and no network. It is
# example data, not the study's results.

# --- Logs ---
*.log

# --- macOS / editors ---
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
